<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rennyo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1415–1499</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rennyo was the eighth head of the Hongan-ji, the main temple of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodo-shinshu">True Pure Land school</a> of Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>. Through preaching tours and simple pastoral letters he spread the faith among farmers and townspeople, above all in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hokuriku-region">Hokuriku region</a>, turning a small sect into a mass movement. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamashina-hongan-ji">Yamashina Hongan-ji</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> and a temple at Ishiyama, later the sect's fortress.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rennyo.jpg" alt="Rennyo" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ブレイズマン · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rennyo5.1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
